# deploy/clagentic-router-update.user.timer — OPT-IN systemd USER timer that
# periodically activates clagentic-router-update.user.service, giving a
# systemd --user deployment a pull-based self-update mechanism (lr-c69197).
# See docs/OPERATOR-GUIDE.md's "Keeping a user-scope host current
# automatically" section for the install sequence and full design
# rationale.
#
# WHY PULL, NOT PUSH (lr-c69197): the crew's post-merge automation
# (clagentic-loadout's post_merge_steps) runs entirely on the crew's own
# host via subprocess.run(shell=False, cwd=root) — no transport, no host
# inventory, no agent on any operator workstation. Standing up a push path
# would mean inventing a remote-exec transport plus long-lived credentials
# into an operator's machine — more moving parts and a larger attack
# surface than reusing the update mechanism that already exists and having
# the target host poll for it on its own schedule.
#
# WHY THIS DOES NOT REBUILD EVERY INTERVAL: "clagentic-router update" itself
# already only rebuilds+installs+restarts when it runs — there is no
# separate lightweight "is a new build available" check invoked first. This
# is a deliberate simplification, not an oversight: the router's discovery
# doctrine (see this repo's CLAUDE.md, "Discover, don't hardcode — but only
# what you can actually verify by calling it") forbids inventing a remote
# "latest revision" discovery endpoint that no code path here has ever
# called — origin/main's HEAD is not queryable through anything this update
# path talks to today, only through `git fetch`+`git log` against
# deploy.source_dir's own origin, which `ensureSourceCheckout` already does
# as its FIRST step on every run. The actual cost of a no-op interval is
# therefore: one `git fetch`+ff-only-pull (cheap, network-bound) that
# reports "already up to date" via git's own exit code, at which point
# `update` proceeds to rebuild from a source tree unchanged from last time.
# A real "skip the build if unchanged" optimization would compare the
# checkout's post-pull HEAD against the INSTALLED binary's own reported
# revision (GET /version or `clagentic-router version`, both linkable via
# lr-92ee18) before deciding to build — that comparison is NOT implemented
# here; it is a real, scoped follow-up (see OPERATOR-GUIDE.md), not silently
# assumed. Today, an idle interval costs one Go compile (seconds, not
# meaningful load for the default interval below) rather than zero.
#
# WHY NO Restart= ON THE PAIRED .service: a failed `update` run (git pull
# rejected, build failure, install/restart readback failure — see
# update.go's runUpdate) must not retry in a tight loop and must not leave
# a half-updated deployment. `update`'s own contract already guarantees the
# second half (a failed build/readback never reaches the install-replace or
# restart step — see clagentic-router-update.user.service's comment); the
# first half (no thrashing) is why this is a plain oneshot with no
# Restart=on-failure of its own — a failure here simply waits for the
# timer's NEXT scheduled activation rather than retrying immediately.
# systemd --user's own default journal captures the failure for later
# inspection (`journalctl --user -u clagentic-router-update`).
#
# DEFAULTS, AND WHY: OnUnitActiveSec=1h with RandomizedDelaySec=10m. An
# hourly cadence is a reasonable balance for a single-operator workstation —
# frequent enough that "the box sat on a stale, previously-widened error
# classification window for 10+ hours with no signal" (the lr-c69197
# incident this exists to close) cannot recur at that scale, infrequent
# enough that a failed run's next attempt isn't itself a thrashing loop.
# RandomizedDelaySec=10m spreads activation instead of firing at exactly
# :00 every hour — immaterial for a single host, but the honest default for
# a template that may be copied to more than one. Both are operator-tunable
# in the installed copy; nothing here is hardcoded beyond this default.

[Unit]
Description=Clagentic: Router self-update timer (user scope)
Documentation=https://github.com/clagentic/clagentic-router

[Timer]
OnStartupSec=15m
OnUnitActiveSec=1h
RandomizedDelaySec=10m
Persistent=true

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
